remony transition". ✓ I read `logs/suite-runs/calib-w1.log:54-90` instead of the summary of it: the failure is at **`:150:59`**, `expect(getByTestId('world-info-note-title')).toHaveText("The Baron's Standard")` **receiving `""`, with the element resolving 14× empty across the full 5 s.** A *persistent* empty is not a near-miss on a budget. ✓ **VERIFIED at source (`WorldInfoNotes.ts:182-188`): `update(null)` sets `root.hidden = true` and RETURNS WITHOUT EVER CLEARING `title.textContent`** — which is written only at `:199` when a real note shows, and starts empty at `:160`. **Two consequences, and the second is the one nobody has been looking at:** (1) `Received ""` proves **no world-info note was EVER shown at any point in that run** — the question is not why the standard's note flickered off; (2) **the assertion is UNSOUND IN THE GREEN DIRECTION** — stale text survives `update(null)`, and `toHaveText` does not require visibility, **so a run in which the note showed earlier and then vanished PASSES ANYWAY.** `:150` does not prove the thing its own test name claims ("then the note persists"). *Every historical green on that line is unproven*, which is why the master makes quantifying it a separate, non-optional deliverable — an eager "fix" to the assertion would have erased the evidence before anyone measured it, so rewriting `:150`/`:151` is firewalled. (D) 🎯 **I HANDED THE RUNNER TWO PRE-DISPROOFS SO IT CANNOT REPEAT THE LAST THREE FIRES' PATTERN OF CHASING A NAMED CANDIDATE.** ✓ The teleport **cannot** land on wrong coordinates: diagnostics `baronStandard.x/.z` (`Game.ts:4326-4327`) read **the very same `baronStandardPosition`** that the note candidate at `:5693` uses. ✓ A rival candidate winning the **distance-first** sort at `:5704` (where `baron_standard`'s top `priority 4` is only a tiebreaker and the *wandering* prospector at radius 1.8 can outrank it) would write a **non-empty** title — so it cannot explain this red, though I kept it on the list as a live latent hazard. My own named candidate **(B) the hero DIES during the 5 s rush** — `stay-for-rush` resumes live combat with the hero teleported beside the standard and standing undefended ⇒ `state.current='dead'` ⇒ the `blocked` clause at `Game.ts:5658` ⇒ persistent empty, and **RNG-driven hence load-independent, matching the closed load finding** — is marked **EXPLICITLY UNPROVEN**, with the exact measurement that kills it if `state.current` is `'playing'` at every sample. (E) 📋 **GOAL REGISTRATION + GUARD DOGFOOD, BOTH ARMS.** Leaf `055-baron-standard-note-diagnosis` landed **in the same commit as the master** (Goal Registration Law), status `queued` and — per the mergeHash-is-a-guard-input law — **deliberately NO `mergeHash`**, so the ancestry arm cannot mistake it for shipped. Both arms then run against it: default → **CLEAR**, `--queue` → **CLEAR**. The master itself is committed, not left untracked (s1120's finding). (F) ✅ **PIPELINE-DRY FOR THE OTHER LANES IS NOW MECHANICALLY VERIFIED, NOT A JUDGEMENT CALL.** `goals.json` holds **exactly 4 non-terminal leaves out of 129**, and every one is accounted for: `rf-34` **blocked, owner design fork**; `cw-02-wrecker-target-premise` **diagnosed** — ✓ I read `reviews/lane-cw-02-wrecker-movement-diagnosis.md:114` and its recommendation is an engine change to `resolveTerrain()` at `Enemy.ts:1252-1264` explicitly "for every caller", i.e. the **F-1118-2 attended/owner class**; `calibrate-suite-workers` **diagnosed** — its re-run is blocked **on the very task I just queued** (F-1107-1 requires dropping or re-deriving 055:121 first, else it is voided again at similar odds); and mine, `queued`. **So authoring a second master would have meant inventing scope, and I did not.** (G) 🧹 **F-1121-2 (fixed here, losslessly): STATUS line 2 was a 122-char TRUNCATED DUPLICATE of the complete s1119 bullet on line 3** — an s1120-era bookkeeping artifact. I verified it was a **strict prefix** of the full bullet before removing it, so the removal provably loses nothing and the complete text is retained. (H) ➡️ **NEXT FIRE, IN ORDER: (1) DRAIN lane-a's `055-baron-standard-note-diagnosis` when the runner finishes it** — expect a **docs-only** final diff (a new `reviews/lane-055-baron-standard-note-diagnosis.md`, optional raws under `artifacts/055-standard-note/`); the firewall's acceptance test is mechanical, `git diff --name-only main...HEAD` must list **ZERO `src/` and ZERO pre-existing `e2e/` files**, so **check that before gating** — temporary instrumentation was permitted and must have been reverted. **(2) Do NOT refill lane-b** — ✓ re-verified myself this fire, unchanged: **25 dirt lines** staged including `.wrangler/tmp/` bundles and the staged **deletion** of `reviews/board-chapter-tab-adoption.md` (on main at `5f7e43e6`); `lane/m4` **0 ahead**; `git -C worktrees/lane-b reset` (mixed — unstages only, deletes nothing) is still the cheap defuse for whoever does the runner restart. (3) lanes c/d idle and **PIPELINE-DRY by proof, per (F)** — not by choice. (4) F-1118-2 and F-1114-1 (`town-t1-square:66`) still want an attended pass; **524 leafless masters remain UNSWEPT** (attended scope). (5) s1120's **566.47 MB** art-staging question and the two other retention findings are still the owner's. **Robin still owes ONE CLEAN RUNNER RESTART** (pid `35584`, up 16d; s1109's fix inert across THIRTEEN fires now). (I) **No merge this fire ⇒ NO gazette item and NO deploy** — the filter law's *"where does the PLAYER see this in a plain boot?"* answers *"nowhere"*: an authored task file and a goal leaf. **TK-01 NOT due, verified independently rather than inherited: `ticker-digest-2026-07-26.md` was compiled TODAY at 06:08 local (`17486be8`), and the daily series is unbroken back to 07-19**; today's coverage compiles tomorrow ≥06:00. `rf-34` untouched. (J) **THE LESSON: s1120 said a measurement is only as true as its denominator. This fire says an ASSERTION is only as true as what it can distinguish.** `toHaveText` on a title that is never cleared cannot tell "the note is showing" from "the note showed once, an hour of game-time ago, and is now hidden" — so the test has been reporting a **strictly weaker fact than its own name** for its whole life, and the red we chased was the *only* honest signal it has ever emitted. **When a flaky test finally fails, check what its green was worth before you make it green again.**
