because two lane batteries were live (Mistake #12): (H1) `blocked` was still true — note `stayForRush()` returns EARLY without ever calling `setPaused(false)` when `securedRunId !== runId`; (H2) the teleport did not land.** **The discriminator is one cheap probe:** at the failure point sample `state.current`, `isPaused`, `baronStandardPlanted`, and `localActor.group.position` alongside `baronStandardPosition` — H1 and H2 disagree on every field. Banked artifacts are gone (later runs wiped `test-results/`), so this needs one fresh red. (E) 🧾 **BOOKKEEPING — three done-moves renamed so no fire hunts for a merge that never existed:** the attended's `m2-05-debt-batch` → `noop-s1108-all-five-already-closed-on-main-*` (**a lawful Mistake-#1-compliant no-op: it wrote WHY, gating 36/36 across both projects and finding all five debt items already fixed on main**), plus the two STOPs above. (F) 📌 **NEXT FIRE, IN ORDER: (1) DRAIN `contract-art-key` off lane-c** (`node scripts/drain-block-check.mjs` FIRST, per §3.0) **and `town-plaza-slot-diagnostics` off lane-a** if they landed; (2) **re-queue rf-37 UNCHANGED the moment the plaza lift merges** — its leaf now carries a DO-NOT-RE-QUEUE-UNTIL marker; (3) **F-1108-2's runner fix — cheapest high-value corrective on the board**; (4) F-1107-2's discriminator once no battery is live; (5) **TK-01 for 2026-07-27 is due AFTER 06:00 tomorrow** — s1106 paid 07-26 today, do not double-pay; (6) the `.claude/skills/drain/SKILL.md` §0 paste, attended-only. (G) **No merge this fire ⇒ no gazette item, no deploy**, per the filter law. Assayer empty, no `CODEX-WALL`, `rf-34` still owner-gated and untouched, all six queues empty at handoff with **two lanes running**. Load closed at **3.65 / 4.95 / 16.34**.
